Notes
The screenshots contain photographed terminal/editor text. SQL has been transcribed and formatted for readability; a few characters in the source images are unclear. Review object names, SQL IDs, dates, XID values, and any environment-specific filters before execution.
1. Session date format
ALTER SESSION SET NLS_DATE_FORMAT = 'DD-MON-YYYY HH24:MI:SS';
2. Active sessions (RAC)
SELECT a.inst_id AS ins,
       a.sid,
       a.serial#,
       a.status,
       a.username,
       a.osuser,
       a.machine,
       TO_CHAR(a.logon_time, 'DD-MON-YY HH24:MI:SS') AS login,
       a.sql_id,
       a.event,
       ROUND(a.last_call_et / 60, 2) AS et_min
FROM   gv$session a,
       gv$sess_io b
WHERE  a.sid = b.sid
AND    a.inst_id = b.inst_id
AND    a.username IS NOT NULL
AND    a.status = 'ACTIVE'
-- AND a.username LIKE '%604872225%'
AND    a.username NOT IN ('GGADMIN', 'GGS_OWNER', 'SYS')
AND    a.sql_id IS NOT NULL
-- AND a.username IN ('AMHOME', 'AMSTAGE', 'SIEBEL')
ORDER BY a.last_call_et / 60 DESC;
